## What was done

A script (capture `p9b-content-f3-apply.py.txt`) read the F3 English table of spec P9-B6 and the 24 F3 rows of
the change list. For each of the 6 weeks it checked each old value against the data, edited the 8 lines of the
D4 step in place (4 en lines and 4 th lines), and proved with a JSON compare that only those 8 values changed.
The Thai values came byte for byte from the change list. The 10 moved rows were checked as byte swaps.
The result is the capture `p9b-content-f3-attempt-diff.txt` (48 line edits, 6 files).

## Why the role stopped

The F3 test file with the edit in place: 5 pass, 6 fail (F3-order weeks 2 to 7).
Every one of the 6 failures is the same problem. The Red test pins `en.teacherLanguage[1]` and `[2]`
without the outer quote characters. Example for week 2:

    expected: Count the ducks. How many? Three!
    data:     "Count the ducks. How many? Three!"      (the quotes are part of the string)

The order check, the th-shape check, and the scope check pass with the quoted lines.

The pinned form contradicts the local style and the Thai twin:
- All 1438 `teacherLanguage` lines of w01 to w08 are wrapped in quote characters (0 unquoted).
  The manual renders them as quotes (`tm-language-quote`).
- The Thai twins in the change list keep their quotes (rows T2, T3, T6, T7, and the others), and the
  F3-th-shape case needs those Thai lines byte equal to the baseline. An English line without quotes next to
  a Thai line with quotes would break the pair.
- Spec P9-B6 shows the two lines as `"Count the ducks. How many? Three!", then "Trace the words: How many?"`.
  The quotes in the cell are the spoken-line quotes of the data. The Red role read them as delimiters.

The rule of the role: a committed Red test is immutable, and a Red test that contradicts the specification or
the local style gives a blocked result that requests a Mid Red retry. The role did not drop the quotes to make
the test pass. The role restored w02 to w07 with `git checkout`. The tree is clean again. Nothing was committed
and nothing was staged.

